- BLOUSE: cream ground with blue sparrows and vines. This is a separate fabric from the saree body and from the pallu.

PLACEMENT MAP (seen from behind):
1. BLOUSE fabric: the back neckline, the right shoulder and both sleeves. Plain blouse fabric. Most of the blouse back is covered by the spread pallu.
2. PALLU print: the pallu comes over the top of the left shoulder from the front and is opened out flat to its FULL WIDTH across the back, unpleated, like a panel on display. It covers the back from the left shoulder across to the right hip and hangs down to mid-calf. This spread panel, and only this panel, is cream PALLU print. The whole pallu design is visible in one piece: the blue vine band section nearest the shoulder, the peacock complete and unbroken across the middle, and the scalloped bell-motif edge along the very bottom.
3. BODY print: everything else visible from behind: the back of the skirt below and beside the spread pallu, from the waist to the hem, and both sides of the body. Deep blue BODY print with no peacock, no pallu motif and no cream pallu ground on it.
4. BORDER: along the hem, and along both long edges of the spread pallu, exactly as narrow as shown. The end edge of the pallu, the edge where the saree finishes, has NO border: the scalloped bell-motif edge is the fabric's end.
